    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change moves the owner's date-derived values onto a **fiscal-year basis** (fiscal year starts 1 July), all keyed off the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`.\n\n**New helper \u2014 `rest/function/common/FiscalYear.java`**\nThe single definition of the fiscal-year basis, so the three consumers can't drift apart:\n- `of(date)` \u2192 four-digit fiscal year (a date on/after 1 July belongs to that calendar year; before 1 July, the previous year).\n- `yy(date)` \u2192 two-digit fiscal year (membership number's year segment).\n- `label(date)` \u2192 `FY<YY>` (e.g. `FY26`).\n- `between(start, end)` \u2192 whole elapsed fiscal years (tenure).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- `membershipNumber` year segment now uses `FiscalYear.yy(...)` instead of the raw calendar year \u2014 this is the behaviour change to the membership identifier.\n- Added the new `fiscalYear` mapping \u2192 `FiscalYear.label(...)`.\n- Tenure in `membershipPoints` now counts elapsed fiscal years (`FiscalYear.between(...) > 1`) instead of a 365-day window; dropped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**\n- Added the read-only `fiscalYear` field (`FY<YY>`) to the owner schema (generates the DTO getter/setter).\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to state the fiscal-year basis.\n\n**Convention note:** I named the fiscal year by the calendar year in which it *begins* (1 Jul 2026 \u2013 30 Jun 2027 = `FY26`). The spec left `FY<YY>` ambiguous between start- and end-year naming; the test only checks the `FY\\d{2}` shape, so it passes either way, but I picked one convention and applied it consistently across all three derived values.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green (the `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsFiscalYear` check for `FY\\d{2}` passes, and the audit log confirms `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26` for a 2026-09-29 registration).\n\nThis is not a git repository, so I made no commit \u2014 let me know if you'd like me to initialize one.",
